Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: DriveSync
Upstream-Contact: Rafael Tosta (https://github.com/rafatosta)
Source: https://github.com/rafatosta/drivesync
Comment: DriveSync itself is under the GNU General Public License version 3 only. The program is one Rust binary that
 also links the crates in vendor/ (298, listed below by the licence each one's Cargo.toml states; all of them can be
 combined with GPL-3.0-only). The stanzas of vendor/ are generated (sparky-os/packages/drivesync/debian/gen-copyright.py
 in the edition's build repository) from the table debian/crate-licences.tsv, which pins every crate's legal files by
 SHA-256; the files themselves (they carry their authors' names and addresses) are not kept in git, build.sh takes them
 from the vendor tree and stops unless each has the pinned hash, and they are installed in
 /usr/share/doc/drivesync/vendor-licences. The build stops when this file differs from what the generator gives.

